From 22f506cd945e009e11ad4c952738f7c026253949 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: b70-notes <b70-notes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/21] Inkling DSpark: optional reduced-vocabulary draft head;
 draft ids come back in the chain-state rows

A drafter GGUF with dspark_out_sub (target lm-head rows of N tokens, Q8_0), dspark_markov_w1_sub and
dspark_out_sub_ids (made by scripts/make-dspark-subvocab.py, N = 32768 from Inkling's own answers,
which use 10.8k distinct tokens) runs each chained position's lm-head pass over those rows (80 MB instead of
492 MB), takes the argmax in the subset and writes the full token id into element `rank` of the position's
chain-state row. The driver reads the ids from h_nextn and requests a logits row only for the anchor, so the
6.4 MB block logits copy and the host argmax over 200k disappear. LLAMA_DSPARK_SUB=0 = full head.
Uncensored AD-Q4_K, n-max 1: draft 2.43 -> 1.27 ms, step 26.6 -> 25.4 ms; temp-0 acceptance n-max 2 0.487 vs 0.494.

Co-Authored-By: otaliptus <56600661+otaliptus@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
